{%- comment -%}
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RELEASE CALENDAR (custom vcollect)

Custom (not Impact): a release calendar as a real data table.

Generative engines extract tables close to verbatim, so the value of this section is the markup, not the styling:
<caption> naming the table, <thead> separated from <tbody>, and a scope on every header cell. That is what lets a machine
tell which value belongs to which column without guessing from the layout.

The rows are emitted in chronological order server-side, so the order a crawler reads is the useful one even though it
never runs the sorting script. assets/custom-sortable-table.js only lets a human reorder what is already there.

Editorial content lives entirely in the blocks: nothing about a release is hardcoded here.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
{%- endcomment -%}

<script type="module" src="{{ 'custom-sortable-table.js' | asset_url }}"></script>

{%- liquid
  comment
    Chronological default order. Liquid's `sort` filter cannot sort blocks on a nested settings path, so each block is
    reduced to a "date::index" entry and the list of entries is sorted instead. ISO dates sort lexicographically in
    exactly the same order as chronologically, which is the whole reason the setting is stored as YYYY-MM-DD.

    A block with no date sorts first as an empty string, so those are rendered after the dated ones on purpose: an
    undated row at the top would read as the next release.
  endcomment
  assign dated_rows = ''
  assign undated_rows = ''

  for block in section.blocks
    if block.settings.release_date != blank
      assign dated_rows = dated_rows | append: block.settings.release_date | append: '::' | append: forloop.index0 | append: '|'
    else
      assign undated_rows = undated_rows | append: forloop.index0 | append: '|'
    endif
  endfor

  assign dated_rows = dated_rows | split: '|' | sort
  assign undated_rows = undated_rows | split: '|'
-%}

<div class="container">
  <div class="page-spacer">
    <div class="page">
      <h1 class="h1">{{ page.title | escape }}</h1>

      {%- render 'content-freshness' -%}

      {%- if section.settings.lede != blank -%}
        <div class="prose citable-lede">{{ section.settings.lede }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
        {%- comment -%} tabindex makes the horizontal scroll of a wide table reachable without a pointer {%- endcomment -%}
        <sortable-table class="citable-table-wrapper" tabindex="0">
          <table class="citable-table">
            <caption>{{ section.settings.table_caption | escape }}</caption>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col" data-sort-type="text">{{ 'calendar.columns.set' | t }}</th>
                <th scope="col" data-sort-type="text">{{ 'calendar.columns.language' | t }}</th>
                <th scope="col" data-sort-type="date">{{ 'calendar.columns.release_date' | t }}</th>
                <th scope="col">{{ 'calendar.columns.products' | t }}</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {%- comment -%}
                `| plus: 0` is not cosmetic: splitting a string yields strings, and an array lookup in Liquid needs a
                number. Without the conversion section.blocks["3"] resolves to nil and the row renders empty.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- for entry in dated_rows -%}
                {%- assign entry_parts = entry | split: '::' -%}
                {%- assign block_index = entry_parts[1] | plus: 0 -%}
                {%- render 'release-calendar-row', block: section.blocks[block_index] -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
              {%- for entry in undated_rows -%}
                {%- assign block_index = entry | plus: 0 -%}
                {%- render 'release-calendar-row', block: section.blocks[block_index] -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </sortable-table>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.notes != blank -%}
        <div class="prose">{{ section.settings.notes }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Release calendar",
  "class": "shopify-section--release-calendar",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Custom (not Impact). One block per release. Rows are ordered by release date automatically: the order of the blocks in this list does not matter. The last-review date shown on the page comes from the page's \"Date de mise à jour\" field, not from a setting here."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "lede",
      "label": "Opening paragraph",
      "info": "Two to three sentences answering directly what this calendar covers and how often it is updated. This is the block an AI assistant extracts.",
      "default": "<p>[À REMPLIR : deux à trois phrases. Ce que couvre ce calendrier (langues, types de produits), la source des dates, et à quelle fréquence la page est revue.]</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "table_caption",
      "label": "Table caption",
      "info": "Read by screen readers and used by search engines to label the table. Say what the table lists, not \"tableau\".",
      "default": "[À REMPLIR : ex. Dates de sortie officielles des extensions, par langue]"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "notes",
      "label": "Notes below the table",
      "info": "Where the dates come from, and what happens when an official date moves."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "name": "Release",
      "type": "release",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "set_name",
          "label": "Set name",
          "info": "The official name of the extension, exactly as the publisher writes it."
        },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "language",
          "label": "Language",
          "options": [
            { "value": "Japonais", "label": "Japonais" },
            { "value": "Chinois", "label": "Chinois" },
            { "value": "Français", "label": "Français" },
            { "value": "Anglais", "label": "Anglais" },
            { "value": "Coréen", "label": "Coréen" }
          ],
          "default": "Japonais"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "release_date",
          "label": "Release date",
          "info": "ISO format YYYY-MM-DD. Only an officially announced date: leave empty rather than writing an estimate, the row will then be listed after the confirmed ones."
        },
        {
          "type": "product_list",
          "id": "products",
          "label": "Products for this release",
          "limit": 4
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Release calendar"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
